Fix AIKIDO-2026-310861 / GHSA-p6vx-979v-rg4c (CWE-843 type confusion) in seroval-plugins.

The vulnerable code (fromJSON() resolving/rejecting a deserialized Promise node by
passing the raw decoded value straight into the promise resolver without an
isThennable guard) lives entirely in the core `seroval` package's deserializer, not
in seroval-plugins itself. The published seroval-plugins@1.6.0 npm artifact ships only
compiled dist/ bundles (files: ["dist"]) and does not vendor any seroval source, so the
fix cannot be applied as a source edit here.

seroval-plugins is the exploitation vector: it consumes `seroval` as a (peer) dependency
whose "^1.0" range still permits the vulnerable seroval 0.12.0..1.6.1. Upstream fixed the
flaw in seroval 1.6.2 (commits f1ffcc96 core-context + 51ef3a0f binary deserializer) and
released seroval-plugins 1.6.2 carrying only a dependency bump to seroval@1.6.2.

This patch remediates the artifact per its actual contract: it constrains the `seroval`
dependency to the fixed line (>=1.6.2) so a vulnerable core package can no longer satisfy
seroval-plugins' install, and pins the devDependency to 1.6.2 to match upstream 1.6.2.

--- a/package.json
+++ b/package.json
@@ -16,14 +16,14 @@
     "@types/node": "^24.10.0",
     "@vitest/ui": "^4.0.6",
     "esbuild": "^0.28.1",
-    "seroval": "1.6.0",
+    "seroval": "1.6.2",
     "tsdown": "^0.22.14",
     "tslib": "^2.8.1",
     "typescript": "^7.0.2",
     "vitest": "^4.0.6"
   },
   "peerDependencies": {
-    "seroval": "^1.0"
+    "seroval": ">=1.6.2"
   },
   "private": false,
   "description": "Stringify JS values",
